Description: zink makes the image of a dma-buf export with a modifier the driver can render with
 add_resource_bind() gave an image that is about to be exported as a dma-buf
 the one modifier DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR. NVIDIA's Vulkan driver lists linear
 for the format without the colour attachment blend feature that a render
 target needs, so the image could not be made, eglExportDMABUFImageMESA had no
 descriptor to give, and GTK's GtkGraphicsOffload around a GtkGLArea on the
 edition's default zink died with EBADF (ORDER 457).
 .
 Linear is still the choice when its features are the best the driver lists.
 Otherwise the driver is offered the single plane modifiers with the best
 features, and the exported dma-buf carries the one it chose (on the RTX 3060,
 615.71.09: 0x300000000606014).
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-07
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
